; Regression sentinel for bugs #49 / #159 / #166.
;
; This is a verbatim reduction of `test_atoi_neg` from
; `test/MC/MC6809/Execution/Inputs/codegen-stdlib-ctype.ll` — a
; PHI-carried-i16 value live across an i8 byte load + i8 compare.
; Bug #49 fix part 2 added a custom PSHS-D / ... / PULS-D wrap in
; `MC6809InstrInfo::expandCompareImm` to preserve D across the
; byte load (the load clobbers D's low byte). Bug #159 narrowed
; the wrap with a live-out gate; bug #166 then removed the wrap
; after a spike confirmed the underlying PHI clobber no longer
; reproduces (regalloc / spill placer handles it now).
;
; The autogen CHECK lines below are the durable codegen-shape
; sentinel: any future change in this function's emitted asm
; — including the reintroduction of any PSHS-D / PULS-D wrap —
; will diff and fail. Regenerate with
; `update_llc_test_checks.py` only after a deliberate codegen
; change, never as a way to silence an unexpected diff.
;
; The companion execution test
; `test/MC/MC6809/Execution/codegen-stdlib-ctype.s` runs
; `test_atoi_neg("-3")` on USim and verifies the i16 result is
; -3 — that catches the SEMANTIC regression but only while that
; test exists. This lit test is the durable shape-level guard
; that stays even if the execution harness gets refactored away.

